# Sandbox requests for steps 02-05. Start the AppHost first:
#   dotnet run --project src/AppHost/FoodDelivery.AppHost
# Run these from VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
# or copy the URLs into curl.exe.

@waiter = https://localhost:7240
@kitchen = https://localhost:7148

### Waiter calls Kitchen by NAME (https+http://kitchen), never by port
GET {{waiter}}/order

### The configuration service discovery reads (injected by the AppHost)
GET {{waiter}}/debug/discovery

### Kitchen directly, through the DCP proxy port from its launchSettings.json
GET {{kitchen}}/dish-of-the-day

### Step 03: Postgres metadata via the injected connection string (no tables touched)
GET {{kitchen}}/infra/postgres

### Step 03: Redis counter + memory; the count survives AppHost restarts (volume)
GET {{kitchen}}/infra/redis

### Step 03: the connection strings the AppHost injected (passwords masked)
GET {{kitchen}}/debug/connection-strings

### Step 04: one trace across both services. waiterTraceId == fromKitchen.trace.traceId
GET {{waiter}}/order

### Step 04: an error that crosses services (kitchen 500 -> waiter 500); red spans in the dashboard
GET {{waiter}}/order?burn=true

### Step 04: kitchen called directly: no traceparent received, so it starts a NEW trace
GET {{kitchen}}/dish-of-the-day
